<hr>
<p>	Her mother and father, Trilasia and Sundor SlingCaster
        raised Valacian in a grand castle until a young age of sixteen.&nbsp; Sundor was a great
        Dragon with the wisdom and might of a hundred men.&nbsp; Trilasia was a kind and gentle
        Erudite who would do anything to please her family.</p>
        <p>At sixteen years of age Valacian traveled home from school,
        as she did most days, and found that her mother and father were not home to greet her.
        &nbsp; This being an odd occurrence, she scurried about the castle to try and locate her
        parents.&nbsp; With a horrid look in her eyes, Valacian found her mother and father slain,
        lying amongst numerous books in the library where Sundor often read.&nbsp; Valacian fell
        to her knees and sobbed over her mother and fathers death not understanding why such a thing could happen. It
        seems as though only creatures with an evil and bloody heart must have been responsible
        for the deaths of her parents.</p>
        <p>After a few months of grieving, Valacian decided she wanted
        to learn more about why her parents were so brutally murdered.&nbsp; With the will and
        strength which her great father once had, she stepped back into the library and searched
        for clues.&nbsp; The torn books, which were scattered amongst the bodies, were that of a
        language she did not understand.</p>
        <p>Titles such as the Wizards Cannon were found on the covers
        of books. In fact, most books revolved around Arcane Science and were of a different
        language. Arcane Science was a subject lightly touched upon during her early school years
        and was studied by Wizards in the vast lands of Norrath. She gathered some of the books
        and decided to take it to a great Wizard Guild Master.&nbsp; Days were spent with the
        mighty Wizard as they read the books together.&nbsp; She was told the book was written in
        Old Erudin, a language used by mastered Wizards.&nbsp; As she studied the books, she
        learned a little about the skills of a Wizard and the language it was scribed in.
        &nbsp; From this moment on, Valacian knew what her destiny was.&nbsp; Valacian was
        destined to be a mighty Wizard.&nbsp; She would use her skills and strengths as a Wizard
        and locate the murderers of her parents!</p>
<p>
        Valacian spent a lot of days gaining experience with her new found powers, studying the
        Arcane Science while removing creatures of evil heart from Norrath.&nbsp; Now having
        attained her 29th circle of power, she decided to form and lead a new family&nbsp; one
        that would assist her in cleansing the world from evil hearted creatures.&nbsp; Her new
        family would be named after her fathers race and would represent the true power all
        her friends bestowed.&nbsp; The name would be Dragons Claw.&nbsp; Dragons Claw would be a
        force well known within the lands of Norrath and those of an evil heart would be cleansed
        from the lands.&nbsp; Valacian and her new family would find the murderers of her parents
        one day and a great celebration would come forth upon all that is good.</p>
